                                                   '          <h2 class="cs-heading-2">2. Constitutional Parity: '
                                                   'Government Recruitments, UPSC & PSUs</h2>\n'
                                                   '          <p>A frequent myth is that online degrees are '
                                                   'disqualified from government civil service examinations, public '
                                                   'sector units (PSUs), and state administrative positions. Under '
                                                   'Indian administrative law, this myth is completely unfounded:</p>\n'
                                                   '\n'
                                                   '          <ul class="cs-checklist" style="list-style: none; '
                                                   'padding: 0; margin: 16px 0;">\n'
                                                   '            <li style="padding: 10px 0; display: flex; '
                                                   'align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;">\n'
                                                   '              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" '
                                                   'fill="none" stroke="#0a6d6f" stroke-width="2.5" '
                                                   'style="flex-shrink:0; margin-top:2px;"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 '
                                                   '4 12"/></svg>\n'
                                                   '              <span><strong>UPSC & State PSC Eligibility:</strong> '
                                                   'Candidates possessing a UGC-DEB entitled online MBA are 100% '
                                                   'eligible to apply for Union Public Service Commission (Civil '
                                                   'Services IAS/IPS/IRS) and State PSC exams (UPPSC, BPSC, MPSC, '
                                                   'TNPSC, RPSC) wherever a post-graduate qualification is accepted or '
                                                   'required.</span>\n'
                                                   '            </li>\n'
                                                   '            <li style="padding: 10px 0; display: flex; '
